text: >-
  "Bates 003996-R2" is a Bates-stamped discovery exhibit (standard numbering
  used by the

  prosecution/Utah County Attorney's Office when producing large volumes of
  materials to the

  defense). It refers to a video recording (likely bodycam, stationhouse
  interview, or surveillance

  footage) of Tyler Robinson's encounter with law enforcement. The video shows
  him being read

  his Miranda rights at approximately 6:25 p.m. MDT on September 11, 2025 (with
  an internal video

  timestamp around 03:36:53 or similar, depending on the exact frame).

  instagram.com +1

  The exhibit has been referenced in recent defense filings and analysis
  (particularly around late

  March 2026) to highlight alleged timeline discrepancies: Robinson was already
  in custody and

  mirandized (and reportedly invoked his right to counsel) hours before the
  official "surrender"

  narrative and a Discord confession message attributed to him.
  Podcaster/investigator Baron

  Coleman has prominently discussed and quoted from it in his coverage.
  timesofindia.indiatimes.com
